#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:1
msgid "Cookbook"
msgstr "配方集"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:3
msgid ""
"Short, working answers to tasks that come up again and again. Each recipe is"
" self-contained; the guides explain the reasoning behind the rules."
msgstr "针对反复出现的任务给出简短、可运行的答案。每个配方自成一体；规则背后的理由见各指南。"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:6
msgid "Rolling metrics for one series"
msgstr "单条序列的滚动指标"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:8
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"#include <fincore/rolling_engine.hpp>\n"
"\n"
"fincore::rolling_engine engine{returns, std::nullopt, 60U, 252.0};\n"
"const auto series = engine.compute({fincore::rolling_metric::sharpe,\n"
"                                    fincore::rolling_metric::volatility,\n"
"                                    fincore::rolling_metric::max_drawdown});"
"\n"
"for (const auto& [name, frame] : series) {\n"
"    const auto& values = frame.get_column<double>(fincore::returns_column);\n"
"    // values.size() == returns.shape().first - 60 + 1\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"#include <fincore/rolling_engine.hpp>\n"
"\n"
"fincore::rolling_engine engine{returns, std::nullopt, 60U, 252.0};\n"
"const auto series = engine.compute({fincore::rolling_metric::sharpe,\n"
"                                    fincore::rolling_metric::volatility,\n"
"                                    fincore::rolling_metric::max_drawdown});"
"\n"
"for (const auto& [name, frame] : series) {\n"
"    const auto& values = frame.get_column<double>(fincore::returns_column);\n"
"    // values.size() == returns.shape().first - 60 + 1\n"
"}\n"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:21
msgid ""
"The output starts at the first **complete** window, so it is shorter than "
"the input by `window - 1` rows. Pass a benchmark frame as the second "
"argument only if you ask for `rolling_metric::beta`."
msgstr ""
"输出从第一个**完整**窗口开始，因此比输入少 `window - 1` 行。只有在需要 `rolling_metric::beta` "
"时才把基准帧作为第二个参数传入。"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:25
msgid "The deepest drawdowns as a table"
msgstr "把最深的几次回撤列成表"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:27
#, python-brace-format, python-format
msgid ""
"#include <fincore/metrics/drawdown.hpp>\n"
"\n"
"for (const auto& row : fincore::gen_drawdown_table(returns, 5U, "
"\"returns\")) {\n"
"    if (std::isnan(row.net_drawdown_percent)) {\n"
"        continue;  // unused row: fewer than five episodes in the series\n"
"    }\n"
"    std::printf(\"%.2f%%  peak %lld  valley %lld\\n\",\n"
"                row.net_drawdown_percent,\n"
"                static_cast<long long>(*row.peak),\n"
"                static_cast<long long>(*row.valley));\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"#include <fincore/metrics/drawdown.hpp>\n"
"\n"
"for (const auto& row : fincore::gen_drawdown_table(returns, 5U, "
"\"returns\")) {\n"
"    if (std::isnan(row.net_drawdown_percent)) {\n"
"        continue;  // unused row: fewer than five episodes in the series\n"
"    }\n"
"    std::printf(\"%.2f%%  peak %lld  valley %lld\\n\",\n"
"                row.net_drawdown_percent,\n"
"                static_cast<long long>(*row.peak),\n"
"                static_cast<long long>(*row.valley));\n"
"}\n"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:41
msgid ""
"Depth is a **positive** percentage of the prior peak, unlike `max_drawdown`,"
" which returns a negative fraction. When highs tie, the window starts at the"
" latest one."
msgstr "深度是相对前高的**正**百分比，而 `max_drawdown` 返回负数小数。高点并列时，窗口从最新的那个开始。"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:45
msgid "VaR plus a coverage verdict"
msgstr "VaR 加一个覆盖检验结论"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:47
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"#include <fincore/risk/backtesting.hpp>\n"
"#include <fincore/risk/models.hpp>\n"
"\n"
"fincore::risk_forecast_config config;\n"
"config.confidence_level = 0.99;\n"
"\n"
"const auto estimate = fincore::forecast_var(returns, config);\n"
"const auto verdict = fincore::backtest_var(forecast, realized, 0.99, 0.05);\n"
"\n"
"if (estimate.status != fincore::risk_estimate_status::ok) {\n"
"    // insufficient_data or failed: do not report the number as a result\n"
"} else if (verdict.status == fincore::risk_backtest_status::inconclusive) {\n"
"    // fewer than three pairs or fewer than five expected exceptions\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"#include <fincore/risk/backtesting.hpp>\n"
"#include <fincore/risk/models.hpp>\n"
"\n"
"fincore::risk_forecast_config config;\n"
"config.confidence_level = 0.99;\n"
"\n"
"const auto estimate = fincore::forecast_var(returns, config);\n"
"const auto verdict = fincore::backtest_var(forecast, realized, 0.99, 0.05);\n"
"\n"
"if (estimate.status != fincore::risk_estimate_status::ok) {\n"
"    // insufficient_data or failed: do not report the number as a result\n"
"} else if (verdict.status == fincore::risk_backtest_status::inconclusive) {\n"
"    // fewer than three pairs or fewer than five expected exceptions\n"
"}\n"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:64
#, python-format
msgid ""
"`estimate` is negative for losses under the `losses_negative` convention. An"
" `inconclusive` verdict is not a pass: 250 days at 99% expects 2.5 "
"exceptions, below the five needed to test."
msgstr ""
"在 `losses_negative` 约定下 `estimate` 对亏损为负。`inconclusive` 不是通过：250 天 99% 期望 "
"2.5 个例外，低于检验所需的五个。"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:68
msgid "GARCH VaR over a multi-day horizon"
msgstr "多日期限的 GARCH VaR"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:70
msgid ""
"config.method = fincore::risk_forecast_method::garch;\n"
"config.garch_kernel = fincore::garch_model::gjr_garch;\n"
"config.horizon = 10U;\n"
"const auto ten_day = fincore::forecast_var(returns, config);\n"
msgstr ""
"config.method = fincore::risk_forecast_method::garch;\n"
"config.garch_kernel = fincore::garch_model::gjr_garch;\n"
"config.horizon = 10U;\n"
"const auto ten_day = fincore::forecast_var(returns, config);\n"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:77
msgid ""
"Only the GARCH method composes over `horizon`; historical and EVT estimates "
"ignore it. A fit that does not converge returns `failed` with a `note` "
"instead of a number."
msgstr ""
"只有 GARCH 方法会在 `horizon` 上组合；历史法与 EVT 估计忽略它。未收敛的拟合返回带 `note` 的 "
"`failed`，而不是一个数字。"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:81
msgid "Quantile means from a factor panel"
msgstr "从因子面板取分位均值"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:83
#, python-brace-format, python-format
msgid ""
"const auto model = fincore::analyze_factor(prepared, factor_config);\n"
"const auto& table = model.mean_returns_by_quantile;\n"
"\n"
"for (std::size_t q = 0; q < table.quantiles.size(); ++q) {\n"
"    for (std::size_t l = 0; l < table.labels.size(); ++l) {\n"
"        std::printf(\"Q%d %s %.5f\\n\", table.quantiles[q],\n"
"                    table.labels[l].c_str(),\n"
"                    table.means[q * table.labels.size() + l]);\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"const auto model = fincore::analyze_factor(prepared, factor_config);\n"
"const auto& table = model.mean_returns_by_quantile;\n"
"\n"
"for (std::size_t q = 0; q < table.quantiles.size(); ++q) {\n"
"    for (std::size_t l = 0; l < table.labels.size(); ++l) {\n"
"        std::printf(\"Q%d %s %.5f\\n\", table.quantiles[q],\n"
"                    table.labels[l].c_str(),\n"
"                    table.means[q * table.labels.size() + l]);\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:96
msgid ""
"Row keys are quantiles, column keys are labels, and the buffer is row-major."
" Read `labels` from the same table when you save it; a table without its "
"label order is ambiguous."
msgstr "行键是分位、列键是标签，缓冲区按行主序。保存表时把同一张表的 `labels` 一起保存；缺少标签顺序的表是有歧义的。"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:100
msgid "A point-in-time panel from revisions"
msgstr "用修订数据构造时点面板"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:102
msgid ""
"#include <fincore/factor/pit.hpp>\n"
"\n"
"std::vector<fincore::pit_observation> observations{\n"
"    {\"AAA\", {as_of, known_at, effective_from, 1.25}, true},\n"
"    {\"BBB\", {as_of, known_at, effective_from, -0.40}, false},  // out of "
"universe\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"const auto prepared = fincore::prepare_pit_factor_data(\n"
"    observations, prices, evaluation_dates);\n"
"const auto model = fincore::analyze_factor(prepared, factor_config);\n"
msgstr ""
"#include <fincore/factor/pit.hpp>\n"
"\n"
"std::vector<fincore::pit_observation> observations{\n"
"    {\"AAA\", {as_of, known_at, effective_from, 1.25}, true},\n"
"    {\"BBB\", {as_of, known_at, effective_from, -0.40}, false},  // out of "
"universe\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"const auto prepared = fincore::prepare_pit_factor_data(\n"
"    observations, prices, evaluation_dates);\n"
"const auto model = fincore::analyze_factor(prepared, factor_config);\n"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:115
msgid ""
"Ordering is checked, not repaired: `known_at` must not precede `as_of`, and "
"`effective_from` must not precede `known_at`. On each evaluation date an "
"asset contributes the revision with the largest `(effective_from, known_at, "
"as_of)` among those already effective and known; assets outside the universe"
" are skipped silently, which is why a date can have fewer cross-sections "
"than assets."
msgstr ""
"顺序是被检查的，不是被修正的：`known_at` 不得早于 `as_of`，`effective_from` 不得早于 "
"`known_at`。在每个评估日期，资产贡献已生效且已知的修订中 `(effective_from, known_at, as_of)` 最大者；不在"
" universe 中的资产被静默跳过，这就是某一天截面数可能少于资产数的原因。"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:121
msgid "A reproducible simulation"
msgstr "可复现的模拟"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:123
msgid ""
"#include <fincore/simulation/paths.hpp>\n"
"\n"
"const auto paths = fincore::geometric_brownian_motion(\n"
"    100.0,    // initial value\n"
"    0.08,     // annualized drift\n"
"    0.20,     // annualized volatility\n"
"    1.0,      // total years\n"
"    1.0 / 252.0,  // time step\n"
"    1'000U,   // path count\n"
"    42U);     // seed\n"
msgstr ""
"#include <fincore/simulation/paths.hpp>\n"
"\n"
"const auto paths = fincore::geometric_brownian_motion(\n"
"    100.0,    // initial value\n"
"    0.08,     // annualized drift\n"
"    0.20,     // annualized volatility\n"
"    1.0,      // total years\n"
"    1.0 / 252.0,  // time step\n"
"    1'000U,   // path count\n"
"    42U);     // seed\n"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:136
msgid ""
"The same seed reproduces the same frame inside this library. That is a "
"reproducibility guarantee, not a promise of NumPy identity — only functions "
"whose documentation names a reference stream carry that promise."
msgstr "同一 seed 在本库内复现同一帧。这是可复现性保证，不是与 NumPy 一致的承诺 —— 只有文档写明参考流的函数才带这个承诺。"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:140
msgid "Add a table to a report and export it"
msgstr "给报表加一张表并导出"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:142
msgid ""
"fincore::report_section section;\n"
"section.key = \"risk\";\n"
"section.title = \"Risk\";\n"
"\n"
"fincore::report_table table;\n"
"table.key = \"var\";\n"
"table.title = \"VaR by confidence level\";\n"
"table.columns = {\"level\", \"var\", \"verdict\"};\n"
"for (const auto& row : rows) {\n"
"    table.rows.push_back({fincore::report_cell::text_cell(row.level),\n"
"                          fincore::report_cell::number_cell(row.value),\n"
"                          fincore::report_cell::text_cell(row.verdict)});\n"
"}\n"
"section.tables.push_back(std::move(table));\n"
"document.sections.push_back(std::move(section));\n"
"\n"
"const std::string html = fincore::render_html(document, {.language = "
"\"zh\"});\n"
msgstr ""
"fincore::report_section section;\n"
"section.key = \"risk\";\n"
"section.title = \"Risk\";\n"
"\n"
"fincore::report_table table;\n"
"table.key = \"var\";\n"
"table.title = \"VaR by confidence level\";\n"
"table.columns = {\"level\", \"var\", \"verdict\"};\n"
"for (const auto& row : rows) {\n"
"    table.rows.push_back({fincore::report_cell::text_cell(row.level),\n"
"                          fincore::report_cell::number_cell(row.value),\n"
"                          fincore::report_cell::text_cell(row.verdict)});\n"
"}\n"
"section.tables.push_back(std::move(table));\n"
"document.sections.push_back(std::move(section));\n"
"\n"
"const std::string html = fincore::render_html(document, {.language = "
"\"zh\"});\n"

#: ../../site/guides/cookbook.md:162
msgid ""
"`language = \"zh\"` renders the Chinese labels from the same document; the "
"cells you supply are printed as given, so translate your own labels at the "
"call site."
msgstr "`language = \"zh\"` 会用同一文档渲染中文标签；你提供的单元格按原样输出，因此自定义标签要在调用处翻译。"

